Overlay patch 0033: auto-discover a disc image in the data dir on boot.

Reported: "I continue to get asked to select a disc image on every install." The
disc-persistence fix (0028) makes a selected disc survive RELAUNCHES and crashes,
but a fresh install / full delete wipes the app container entirely (iOS
sandboxing -- nothing an app can do), so the stored path AND the disc file are
gone and the picker returns.

This makes the Files drop-off pipeline the real path (charter: "Files-app
drop-off is the entire asset story"): on boot, if no valid disc is configured,
scan the data dir (Documents, per patch 0004) for a valid disc image and use it.
So a disc that survived an app UPDATE is picked up even if the stored path was
lost, and after a delete the user just drops the disc back into the Dusklight
folder via Files -- no picker, no in-app verification navigation. Only a metadata
`iso::inspect` is used (fast, header-only); full hash verification stays with the
prelaunch UI. Non-recursive top-level scan (the disc lives in the data dir root,
next to config.json; texture_replacements/ etc. are skipped).

Placed right after the existing bad-path invalidation (m_Do_main.cpp ~725),
before the empty path forces the prelaunch UI. Clear of every other patch's
hunks (0015 touches this file only near line 568).

2026-10 sync: upstream reworked this block for borealis io locations (bookmarks)
and renamed dvd_path -> dvdLocation/dvdPath; the scan now sits after the
invalidation and before skipPreLaunchUI is read, and uses borealis::io for the
path string. Still needed: upstream's own disc persistence (bookmarks / Documents/
imported, which retired patch 0028) does not cover a fresh install where the user
drops the disc into Documents via Files.

--- a/src/m_Do/m_Do_main.cpp
+++ b/src/m_Do/m_Do_main.cpp
@@ -793,6 +793,38 @@
         dusk::getSettings().backend.isoVerification.setValue(dusk::DiscVerificationState::Unknown);
         forcePreLaunchUI = true;
         saveConfigBeforePrelaunch = true;
+    }
+
+    // Auto-discover a disc in the data dir when none is configured (fresh install,
+    // cleared bad path, or a disc just dropped in via Files). Makes the Files
+    // drop-off pipeline work without the picker, and recovers a disc that survived
+    // an app update even if the stored path was lost. A full delete still wipes the
+    // container (iOS sandboxing), but dropping the disc back into the Dusklight
+    // folder is then enough -- no picker. Metadata-only inspect (header-read, fast);
+    // full hash verification stays with the prelaunch UI.
+    if (dusk::getSettings().backend.isoPath.getValue().empty()) {
+        std::error_code scanEc;
+        const auto dataDir = dusk::data::configured_data_path();
+        std::filesystem::directory_iterator scanIt(dataDir, scanEc);
+        const std::filesystem::directory_iterator scanEnd;
+        for (; !scanEc && scanIt != scanEnd; scanIt.increment(scanEc)) {
+            if (!scanIt->is_regular_file(scanEc)) {
+                continue;
+            }
+            dusk::iso::DiscInfo scanInfo{};
+            if (dusk::iso::inspect(scanIt->path().string().c_str(), scanInfo) ==
+                dusk::iso::ValidationError::Success) {
+                const std::string found = borealis::io::fs_path_to_string(scanIt->path());
+                DuskLog.info("Auto-discovered a valid disc image in the data dir: {}", found);
+                dusk::getSettings().backend.isoPath.setValue(found);
+                dusk::getSettings().backend.isoVerification.setValue(
+                    dusk::DiscVerificationState::Unknown);
+                discInfo = scanInfo;
+                forcePreLaunchUI = false;
+                saveConfigBeforePrelaunch = true;
+                break;
+            }
+        }
     }
 
     bool skipPreLaunchUI = dusk::getSettings().backend.skipPreLaunchUI.getValue();
